{"lo":"LO2","title":"The three norths","slides":[{"label":"Title","notes":"Short lesson, but the one everything else rests on. Tell them straight: if they get the three norths wrong, every bearing they take for the rest of the course is wrong. Have a compass and a map extract in front of each cadet.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1920px; height: 12px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 160px; top: 210px; width: 1600px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 34px; align-items: center; text-align: center;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 30px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #275317;\">2434 &#40;Church Fenton&#41; Squadron &#183; Air Training Corps</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 92px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.04; color: #111111; text-wrap: balance;\">Basic Navigation Using<br />Map and Compass</div>\n    <div style=\"width: 340px; height: 5px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 46px; font-weight: 600; color: #501549;\">Learning Outcome 2</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 34px; color: #444444; max-width: 1220px; line-height: 1.35;\">The three norths &#8212; true, grid and magnetic &#8212; and the variation between them</div>\n  </div>\n  \n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"LO2 statement","notes":"Read the outcome out loud. Note the wording is KNOW, not BE ABLE TO - this is understanding, and it gets tested by questions rather than by doing.","bg":"#3a0f34","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1920px; height: 930px; background: #3a0f34;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 200px; top: 260px; width: 1520px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 30px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #c9a6c4;\">Learning Outcome 2</div>\n    <div style=\"width: 200px; height: 5px; background: #ffffff;\"></div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 76px; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.14; text-wrap: pretty;\">Know the different types of north</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"Section: three norths","notes":"Signpost: three norths, then the angle between two of them. Ask before you start whether anyone can name them - most cadets get true and magnetic and miss grid entirely.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1920px; height: 930px; background: #1b3d10;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 200px; top: 320px; width: 1520px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 32px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #a9c9a0;\">Part One</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 96px; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.04;\">Three different norths</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 38px; color: #d5e6d0; max-width: 1240px; line-height: 1.35;\">They point to three different places. Only one of them is any use on a map.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"True North","notes":"Keep this brief. The only thing that matters is that true north exists, it is the spin axis, and it is not what they will use. Cadets who have done geography will want to talk about longitude - let them, then move on.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 76px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #275317;\">The three norths</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 60px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.06;\">True North</div>\n    <div style=\"width: 1680px; height: 4px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 300px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 26px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 36px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.4; max-width: 1500px;\">True North &#8212; and true south &#8212; sit at the geographical poles: the points the Earth actually spins about.</div>\n    <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px 80px;\">\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">The axis of the Earth&#8217;s rotation</span></div>\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">What lines of longitude converge on</span></div>\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">Of almost no practical use to you on an OS map</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; background: #f4f0f4; border-left: 8px solid #501549; padding: 30px 34px;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 27px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #501549;\">Remember</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.38;\">True north is the geographer&#8217;s north. It is not the one you take bearings from.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"Grid North","notes":"This is the slide that earns the lesson. Draw it on the board: curved lines of longitude converging versus a flat regular grid. The two cannot agree, so the grid points at its own north. Then hammer the rule - map work is always grid.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 76px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #275317;\">The three norths</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 60px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.06;\">Grid North</div>\n    <div style=\"width: 1680px; height: 4px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 300px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 26px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 36px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.4; max-width: 1500px;\">The direction every Ordnance Survey map is oriented to. All your map bearings are taken from grid north.</div>\n    <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px 80px;\">\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">The OS grid is an indexing system laid flat over the British Isles</span></div>\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">Grid lines are regular because the map is flat</span></div>\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">Lines of longitude are not &#8212; they close up towards the poles</span></div>\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">So the grid cannot point at the true pole; it points at an imaginary grid north</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; background: #f4f0f4; border-left: 8px solid #501549; padding: 30px 34px;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 27px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #501549;\">The rule</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.38;\">In navigation always use grid north as your reference. True north has no real significance as far as your map is concerned.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"Magnetic North","notes":"The moving pole is the interesting bit - cadets are usually surprised that north is not fixed. Be honest that the 2020 figure of one degree west is from the original lesson and is now out of date; the diagram in the margin of their own map sheet is the authority. That is a genuinely useful habit to teach.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 76px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #275317;\">The three norths</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 60px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.06;\">Magnetic North</div>\n    <div style=\"width: 1680px; height: 4px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 300px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 26px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 36px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.4; max-width: 1500px;\">The direction a compass needle points. The Earth behaves as though a giant magnet lies inside it, north to south.</div>\n    <div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px 80px;\">\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">A freely moving needle lines up with that magnetic field</span></div>\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">The magnetic pole does not sit on the geographical pole</span></div>\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">And it moves &#8212; significantly, in recent years</span></div>\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">In 2014 magnetic north crossed from west of grid north to east, for the first time in the UK since the 1660s</span></div>\n      <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">The change started in the far south-west and is working across the country</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; background: #eff3ed; border-left: 8px solid #275317; padding: 30px 34px;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 27px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #275317;\">Yorkshire, 2020</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.38;\">Magnetic north was 1&#176; west. It was expected to reach zero by 2025 &#8212; so check the current figure on your map sheet.</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"ANIMATION Three Norths","notes":"Run this now, after all three norths have been named. Pause it on the frame where all three are shown together and ask which two the variation sits between. Then let it run on to the drift.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":"Nav LO2 - The Three Norths.html","html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1920px; height: 930px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <a href=\"Nav LO2 - The Three Norths.dc.html\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 140px; top: 150px; width: 1640px; height: 620px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 28px; text-decoration: none; border: 3px solid #275317; padding: 58px 70px; box-sizing: border-box; background: #0b0b0b;\" style-hover=\"background: #131313; border-color: #4b8f34;\">\n    <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 22px;\">\n      <div style=\"width: 18px; height: 18px; background: #4b8f34; border-radius: 50%;\"></div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #4b8f34;\">Animation &#183; play now</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 82px; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.06;\">The Three Norths</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 33px; color: #b9b9b9; line-height: 1.4; max-width: 1300px;\">True, grid and magnetic north drawn on the same diagram, with the variation angle opening and closing between grid and magnetic as it drifts across the decades.</div>\n    <div style=\"margin-top: auto; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 20px; font-size: 30px; font-weight: 600; color: #ffffff;\">\n      <span style=\"border-bottom: 3px solid #4b8f34; padding-bottom: 6px;\">Open the animation</span>\n      <span style=\"color: #4b8f34; font-size: 36px;\">&#8594;</span>\n    </div>\n  </a>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 140px; top: 800px; font-size: 26px; color: #777777;\">Also in the library: <a href=\"index.html\" style=\"color: #4b8f34;\">all 18 navigation animations</a></div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"Section: variation","notes":"Signpost part two. This is the number they will add or subtract for the rest of the course, so it needs to land properly.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 1920px; height: 930px; background: #1b3d10;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 200px; top: 320px; width: 1520px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 32px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #a9c9a0;\">Part Two</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 96px; font-weight: 700; color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.04;\">Magnetic variation</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 38px; color: #d5e6d0; max-width: 1240px; line-height: 1.35;\">The angle between grid north and magnetic north &#8212; and why you cannot ignore it.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"Magnetic variation","notes":"Get them to find the north diagram in the margin of their own map extract. Every OS sheet carries it with the date. That is the number they use, not one they remember from a slide. Point out the diagram exaggerates the angle for clarity - one degree is almost nothing to look at, which is exactly why it gets forgotten.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 76px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #275317;\">Magnetic variation</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 60px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.06;\">The angle between grid and magnetic</div>\n    <div style=\"width: 1680px; height: 4px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 300px; width: 620px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 22px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 33px; font-weight: 600; color: #501549; line-height: 1.34;\">Magnetic variation is the difference, in degrees, between magnetic north and grid north.</div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 29px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 29px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">Grid north is what your map uses</span></div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 29px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 29px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">Magnetic north is what your compass shows</span></div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 29px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 29px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">The variation is the angle between them</span></div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 29px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 29px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">In Yorkshire it was 1&#176; west in 2020</span></div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: baseline;\"><span style=\"color: #275317; font-size: 29px; font-weight: 700;\">&#9656;</span><span style=\"font-size: 29px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.34;\">Always read the current figure off your own sheet</span></div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 790px; top: 292px; width: 990px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 14px;\">\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 900 480\" style=\"width: 962px; height: 513px;\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"True, grid and magnetic north from a common point with the magnetic variation marked\">\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"900\" height=\"480\" fill=\"#ffffff\"></rect>\n      <line x1=\"450\" y1=\"430\" x2=\"450\" y2=\"86\" stroke=\"#999999\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"10 8\"></line>\n      <line x1=\"450\" y1=\"430\" x2=\"398\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"6\"></line>\n      <line x1=\"450\" y1=\"430\" x2=\"321\" y2=\"105\" stroke=\"#275317\" stroke-width=\"6\"></line>\n      <path d=\"M 450 68 l -10 22 l 20 0 Z\" fill=\"#999999\"></path>\n      <path d=\"M 398 72 l -13 23 l 22 -5 Z\" fill=\"#501549\"></path>\n      <path d=\"M 321 89 l -15 21 l 23 -9 Z\" fill=\"#275317\"></path>\n      <path d=\"M 386.7 270.1 A 172 172 0 0 1 424.0 260.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#111111\" stroke-width=\"3\"></path>\n      <line x1=\"382.7\" y1=\"278.1\" x2=\"336\" y2=\"298\" stroke=\"#111111\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n      <circle cx=\"450\" cy=\"430\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#111111\"></circle>\n      <g font-family=\"'Aptos', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif\">\n        <text x=\"478\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"30\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#777777\">TRUE NORTH</text>\n        <text x=\"398\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"32\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#501549\" text-anchor=\"middle\">GRID NORTH</text>\n        <text x=\"297\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"32\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#275317\" text-anchor=\"end\">MAGNETIC NORTH</text>\n        <text x=\"328\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"29\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111111\" text-anchor=\"end\">MAGNETIC VARIATION</text>\n        <text x=\"328\" y=\"328\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#555555\" text-anchor=\"end\">1&#176; west &#183; Yorkshire, 2020</text>\n      </g>\n    </svg>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 25px; color: #666666; text-align: center; line-height: 1.3;\">Angles exaggerated &#8212; one degree is almost invisible at this scale</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"Why variation matters","notes":"This is the bridge to LO3. Do not teach the add-or-subtract rule yet - just establish that map and ground speak different languages and the variation is the translation. If someone asks which way round, tell them that is the next lesson.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 76px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #275317;\">Magnetic variation</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 60px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.06;\">Why it matters</div>\n    <div style=\"width: 1680px; height: 4px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 460px; width: 1680px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 40px;\">\n      <div style=\"background: #f4f0f4; border-top: 8px solid #501549; padding: 36px 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;\">\n        <div style=\"font-size: 25px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #501549;\">Map work</div>\n        <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.14;\">Grid bearings</div>\n        <div style=\"font-size: 28px; color: #555555; line-height: 1.36;\">Anything you measure or plot on the map is a grid bearing.</div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #f4f0f4; border-top: 8px solid #501549; padding: 36px 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;\">\n        <div style=\"font-size: 25px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #501549;\">Ground work</div>\n        <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.14;\">Magnetic bearings</div>\n        <div style=\"font-size: 28px; color: #555555; line-height: 1.36;\">Anything you set on the compass and walk is a magnetic bearing.</div>\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"background: #f4f0f4; border-top: 8px solid #501549; padding: 36px 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;\">\n        <div style=\"font-size: 25px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #501549;\">Between them</div>\n        <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.14;\">The variation</div>\n        <div style=\"font-size: 28px; color: #555555; line-height: 1.36;\">Convert every time you move from one to the other.</div>\n      </div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 316px; width: 1500px; font-size: 35px; color: #333333; line-height: 1.4;\">One degree sounds like nothing. Over a long leg it is not nothing &#8212; and the error compounds with every other error you make.</div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"On the map sheet","notes":"Pass round a full sheet if you have one so they see the diagram in place rather than cropped. Point out the date printed alongside it - the figure is only valid for that year, and their sheet may be old.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 76px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #275317;\">Magnetic variation</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 60px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.06;\">Why they cannot agree</div>\n    <div style=\"width: 1680px; height: 4px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 300px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 16px;\">\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 1240 560\" style=\"width: 1240px; height: 560px;\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A straight map grid laid over a curved Earth, so grid north misses the true pole\">\n      <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1240\" height=\"560\" fill=\"#ffffff\"></rect>\n      <clipPath id=\"gclip\"><circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"460\" r=\"300\"></circle></clipPath>\n      <g clip-path=\"url(#gclip)\">\n        <circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"460\" r=\"300\" fill=\"#eef5fa\"></circle>\n        <path d=\"M 380 160 Q -52 340 380 760\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 380 160 Q 56 340 380 760\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 380 160 Q 164 340 380 760\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 380 160 Q 272 340 380 760\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 380 160 Q 380 340 380 760\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 380 160 Q 488 340 380 760\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 380 160 Q 596 340 380 760\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 380 160 Q 704 340 380 760\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 380 160 Q 812 340 380 760\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 211.19241723192647 212 Q 380 236 548.8075827680735 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 152.87888693474576 264 Q 380 288 607.1211130652542 264\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 116.81945360646432 316 Q 380 340 643.1805463935357 316\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 94.45490723880403 368 Q 380 392 665.545092761196 368\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path><path d=\"M 82.6786250536299 420 Q 380 444 677.32137494637 420\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8fb4d8\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"></path>\n      </g>\n      <circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"460\" r=\"300\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#9fb4c4\" stroke-width=\"3\"></circle>\n      <g transform=\"translate(440 320) rotate(-8)\">\n        <rect x=\"-72\" y=\"-56\" width=\"144\" height=\"112\" fill=\"#f4f0f4\" fill-opacity=\"0.9\"></rect>\n        <line x1=\"-72\" y1=\"-56\" x2=\"-72\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line><line x1=\"-36\" y1=\"-56\" x2=\"-36\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"-56\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line><line x1=\"36\" y1=\"-56\" x2=\"36\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line><line x1=\"72\" y1=\"-56\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line><line x1=\"-72\" y1=\"-56\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"-56\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line><line x1=\"-72\" y1=\"-28\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"-28\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line><line x1=\"-72\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line><line x1=\"-72\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line><line x1=\"-72\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"72\" y2=\"56\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"></line>\n        <rect x=\"-72\" y=\"-56\" width=\"144\" height=\"112\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"></rect>\n      </g>\n      <line x1=\"440\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"349\" y2=\"78\" stroke=\"#777777\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-dasharray=\"11 8\"></line>\n      <line x1=\"440\" y1=\"320\" x2=\"407\" y2=\"82\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"6\"></line>\n      <path d=\"M 349 74 l -4 24 l 20 -12 Z\" fill=\"#777777\"></path>\n      <path d=\"M 407 76 l -13 23 l 22 -5 Z\" fill=\"#501549\"></path>\n      <circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"160\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#111111\"></circle>\n      <circle cx=\"440\" cy=\"320\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#111111\"></circle>\n      <g font-family=\"'Aptos', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif\">\n        <text x=\"404\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"27\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111111\">the true pole</text>\n        <text x=\"300\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#777777\" text-anchor=\"end\">TRUE NORTH</text>\n        <text x=\"300\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#999999\" text-anchor=\"end\">towards the pole</text>\n        <text x=\"436\" y=\"52\" font-size=\"28\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#501549\">GRID NORTH</text>\n        <text x=\"436\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#7d4a74\">along the grid</text>\n        <text x=\"560\" y=\"372\" font-size=\"25\" font-weight=\"600\" fill=\"#501549\">the map grid</text>\n        <line x1=\"556\" y1=\"364\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"344\" stroke=\"#501549\" stroke-width=\"2\"></line>\n        <text x=\"820\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"31\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111111\">The grid is straight</text>\n        <text x=\"820\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"31\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111111\">and parallel.</text>\n        <text x=\"820\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"31\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111111\">The meridians converge</text>\n        <text x=\"820\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"31\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#111111\">on the pole.</text>\n        <text x=\"820\" y=\"444\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#555555\">They cannot both point north &#8212; so</text>\n        <text x=\"820\" y=\"480\" font-size=\"27\" fill=\"#555555\">the grid points at its own north.</text>\n      </g>\n    </svg>\n    <div style=\"font-size: 26px; color: #666666; text-align: center;\">A flat grid laid over a curved Earth &#8212; grid north misses the true pole</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"},{"label":"Recap","notes":"Go round the room rather than taking hands. All three answers are short. If they can name the norths but cannot find the variation on the sheet, the lesson has not landed - go back to the margin diagram before you finish.","bg":"#ffffff","anim":null,"html":"\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 76px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #275317;\">Learning Outcome 2</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 60px; font-weight: 700; color: #111111; line-height: 1.06;\">Can you answer these three?</div>\n    <div style=\"width: 1680px; height: 4px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 120px; top: 300px; width: 1680px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 30px; align-items: center; background: #f4f0f4; padding: 22px 36px;\">\n      <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 52px; font-weight: 700; color: #501549; min-width: 74px;\">1</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 36px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.28;\">Name the three norths, and say which one your map uses.</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 30px; align-items: center; background: #f4f0f4; padding: 22px 36px;\">\n      <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 52px; font-weight: 700; color: #501549; min-width: 74px;\">2</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 36px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.28;\">Which two norths does the magnetic variation sit between?</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; gap: 30px; align-items: center; background: #f4f0f4; padding: 22px 36px;\">\n      <div style=\"font-family: 'Aptos Display', 'Source Sans 3', sans-serif; font-size: 52px; font-weight: 700; color: #501549; min-width: 74px;\">3</div>\n      <div style=\"font-size: 36px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.28;\">Where on your map do you find the current variation?</div>\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; margin-top: 8px;\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 30px; color: #666666;\">Next: <strong style=\"color: #275317;\">Learning Outcome 3 &#8212; using the compass</strong></div>\n      <a href=\"index.html\" style=\"font-size: 28px; font-weight: 600; color: #501549;\">Animation library &#8594;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 100px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #501549;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 50px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #000000;\"></div>\n  <div style=\"position: absolute; left: 0; bottom: 0px; width: 1920px; height: 50px; background: #275317;\"></div>\n  <img src=\"media/crest-t226.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"position: absolute; left: 904px; bottom: 0px; width: 113px; height: 150px;\" />\n"}],"prompts":[{"key":"lo2-p1","afterSlide":5,"text":"Name the three norths, and say which one your map uses."},{"key":"lo2-p2","afterSlide":8,"text":"Why can the grid not point at the true pole? Explain it as you would to a new cadet."},{"key":"lo2-p3","afterSlide":10,"text":"What is magnetic variation, and where do you find the current figure?"},{"key":"lo2-p4","afterSlide":5,"type":"choice","options":["True North","Grid North","Magnetic North","Whichever one is closest"],"answer":"Magnetic North","draft":true,"text":"Your compass needle settles. Which north is it pointing at?"},{"key":"lo2-p5","afterSlide":10,"type":"number","unit":"°","placeholder":"e.g. 3","answer":"2","tolerance":0,"draft":true,"needs":"Practice map sheet","text":"Look at the magnetic variation diagram on the practice map sheet. How many degrees west of Grid North is Magnetic North?"},{"key":"lo2-p6","afterSlide":10,"type":"task","draft":true,"needs":"Practice map sheet","text":"Show your instructor where the variation diagram is on the practice map sheet. Tick it off once they have seen it."}],"printables":[{"file":"practice-map.html","label":"Practice map sheet","note":"One per cadet · A4 · print at 100%, not fit-to-page"}]}